The choice method is of course to have your pet archon 
kill him, there's no debate about that.  However, 
searching for polytraps in the lower mines can be very 
dangerous; they have a tendency of, well, polymorphing 
gnomes/dwarves into quite tough guys.  I prefer to go 
in the deeper mines only very well prepared, which includes 
some chit-chat with my deity about protection and crowns 
and such.  Hence, zapping a priest 3 or 4 times with 
a wand of cold from outside (maybe following a potion 
of paralysis) seems to me to be much less risky than 
diving into the mines and hoping for a trap with the 
potential to send me arch liches and such.  But maybe 
this is a matter of taste.  

